## Parameterized Enums

### Option[T] — The Most Common Generic Enum
```xiom
pub type Option[T] = enum {
  Some(value: T),
  None,
}

let x: Option[Int] = Some(42);
let y: Option[Str] = None();
```

### Result[T, E] — Two Type Parameters
```xiom
pub type Result[T, E] = enum {
  Ok(value: T),
  Err(error: E),
}

fn divide(a: Int, b: Int) -> Result[Int, Str] {
  if b == 0 { return Err("division by zero"); }
  return Ok(a / b);
}
```

### Custom Generic Enums
```xiom
pub type Tree[T] = enum {
  Leaf(value: T),
  Branch(left: Tree[T], right: Tree[T]),
}

pub type Response[T] = enum {
  Success(data: T, status: Int),
  Redirect(url: Str),
  Error(code: Int, message: Str),
}
```

### Pattern Matching Generic Enums
```xiom
fn unwrap_or[T](opt: Option[T], default: T) -> T {
  match opt {
    Some(v) => v,
    None => default,
  }
}
```

